---
ord-format: "0.1"
---

# Drivers
**Acme Cloud | three-year subscription operating plan**

The business sells annual-workflow software to small service companies. The plan begins with 1,200 customers and expands acquisition while improving revenue per account. All monetary amounts are dollars.

The base case assumes month-end customer counts contribute a full month of recurring revenue. Payroll steps up annually; acquisition spending grows with the planned number of new accounts.

| Input || Value |
| --- || --- |
| Opening customers || 1200 |
| New customers per month || 65 |
| Monthly churn rate || 0.025 {:.1%} |
| Monthly revenue per customer || 85 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Gross margin || 0.82 {:.1%} |
| Acquisition cost per customer || 420 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Monthly acquisition growth || 0.018 {:.1%} |
| Annual price growth || 0.04 {:.1%} |
| Monthly payroll || 64000 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Annual payroll growth || 0.08 {:.1%} |
| Monthly overhead || 15000 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Opening cash || 650000 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Organic share || 0.35 {:.1%} |
| Referral share || 0.2 {:.1%} |
| Trial conversion || 0.24 {:.1%} |

# Acquisition Plan
**Demand generation and account acquisition**

Organic and referral channels are expected to supply 55% of new customers. Paid acquisition fills the remaining requirement. Trial volumes are sized from the conversion assumption, and spending includes the fully loaded cost across channels.

